ToolTalk: take TLI's answer to T_NEGOTIATE as a success.

ToolTalk sets TCP_NODELAY on its TLI endpoints with t_optmgmt(T_NEGOTIATE)
and takes anything but T_SUCCESS in the answer's flags as a failure,
printing "t_optmgmt: No Error" for each connection.  TLI's t_optmgmt
answers T_NEGOTIATE with the negotiated options and T_NEGOTIATE in flags;
only an answer to T_CHECK carries T_SUCCESS or T_FAILURE.  Amix's TCP
answers so, with the option set (level IPPROTO_TCP, TCP_NODELAY, value 1).
Either answer is now a success.

--- a/lib/tt/lib/mp/mp_rpc_fns.C	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/lib/tt/lib/mp/mp_rpc_fns.C	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -65,7 +65,10 @@
 	resp.opt.buf = (char *)&reqbuf;
 	resp.opt.maxlen = sizeof (reqbuf);
 
-	if (t_optmgmt(fd, &req, &resp) < 0 || resp.flags != T_SUCCESS) {
+	/* TLI answers T_NEGOTIATE with the negotiated options and T_NEGOTIATE
+	 * in flags; only a T_CHECK answer carries T_SUCCESS or T_FAILURE */
+	if (t_optmgmt(fd, &req, &resp) < 0 ||
+	    (resp.flags != T_SUCCESS && resp.flags != T_NEGOTIATE)) {
 		t_error("t_optmgmt");
 		return (0);
 	}
